[Info   :WT Mouse Aim] WT Mouse Aim v0.55.0 loaded (world follow-point chase w/ body-frame roll-then-pull law [roll the lift vector onto the target, then pull up into it] + signed/clamped pull gate (no bunt) + yaw ease-down on big turns + pitch anti-overshoot brake + bank-servo azimuth deadband (anti fine-cone roll wobble) + roll-rate-smoothed damping (anti high-speed roll-PIO limit cycle) + fine integrator + per-axis manual override (anomaly logging suspended while you're on the stick) + Win32 raw mouse + 3rd-person orbit-camera override w/ hysteretic pole-stable horizon leveling + RMB free-look that keeps our orbit pivot (no snap) and eases the view back to your flight direction on release + AoA-true Fly Level toggle [F7] + phase/maneuver instrumentation + anomaly logging + all-aircraft control (fixed-wing + rotorcraft/VTOL, opt-out via ControlRotorcraft) + master ON/OFF hotkey [F10] + clean reticle-only HUD by default (debug readouts behind ShowDebugHud) + adjustable 3rd-person camera position (distance/height/side offsets) + 'I broke it, fix it please' reset-to-defaults button + measured-reactive LOADED-turn assist [shifts a weak-rudder side correction into a steep bank + real G-pull and fades the dead rudder out; the bank target is sized from a turn-RATE so it self-scales with airspeed (a small high-speed nudge commands the steep loaded bank that actually slews the nose), self-adapting per airframe/speed, no tuning needed] + maneuver recorder hotkey [F8] -> timestamped CSV for tuning across aircraft (now tagged with the active control law per row) + A/B control-law toggle [F9] switching Legacy<->EvolvedLegacy in flight (v0.42: EvolvedLegacy is now the DEFAULT/graduated law = universal atan(ωV/g) bank at all speeds/regimes + final-leg align-hold so the roll-to-align contribution persists until the target is genuinely close laterally, preventing the early wings-level-and-stop-short that Legacy shows in the final few degrees; v0.42 also lowered AssistTurnRateGain 1.5->0.9 to kill the high-speed eager/back-and-forth bank limit cycle. Legacy kept as the pristine A/B reference; BankToTurn abandoned and hidden from the toggle) + regime-aware hover handling (v0.43: on collective aircraft [helis/hover-VTOLs, takeoffDistance==0] EvolvedLegacy ramps from bank-to-turn to yaw-to-point as forward speed drops between HeliForwardSpeed and HeliHoverSpeed [or whenever the game's AutoHover is engaged] — bank is suppressed [wings level] and yaw authority raised by HeliYawScale so the tail rotor points the nose; fixed-wing unchanged) + self-describing recordings & a dedicated anomaly file (v0.44) + widened hover regime band (v0.45: HeliHoverSpeed 20->40, HeliForwardSpeed 60->100 so yaw-to-point stays engaged to higher forward speeds before reverting to bank-to-turn) + true wings-level hover (v0.46: gate the roll-to-align branch by heliBlend too — previously only the bank target was zeroed, so in hover the heli still banked toward the marker [roll] while yaw also swung the nose; now at full hover roll is a pure leveler and yaw alone points the nose) + wider hover-regime defaults/ranges (v0.47: HeliForwardSpeed default 150 so yaw-to-point covers the whole normal heli envelope; HeliForwardSpeed range now up to 300 and HeliHoverSpeed up to 150) + cursor-handoff fix (v0.48: toggling the mod OFF mid-flight no longer pops the Windows pointer over the game — ReleaseCursor now restores the game's true hidden+locked flight cursor [visible only for a real menu/UI flag] and resyncs CursorManager's private visibility cache so its Refresh() can't no-op against a stale value; new CursorLogging instrument emits a [cursor] line on each regime change) + manual input re-seeds the flight direction (v0.48: while you actively hold the stick/keyboard/pedals the aim marker is dragged onto the nose so the instructor stops pulling you back toward the old aim point [the RMB free-look + manual-stick complaint]; release and it holds the heading you ended on. Toggle via ManualReorients) + global hard handoff 'my controls / your controls' (v0.49: ManualHandoffTime>0 [default 1s] makes ANY manual input fully disable the instructor on ALL axes — you fly the plane directly — until that many seconds after your last input, then it re-engages flying straight ahead on the heading you ended on; the fix for 'the instructor still carries some control while I fly manually'. Set 0 for the old per-axis blend) + aim-preserving manual corrections (v0.50: manual input only re-seeds the marker while FREE-LOOKING [RMB/Free Look held]; while aiming, the marker stays on your mouse target — you roll-correct or pull, release, and the instructor resumes toward what you were aiming at, WT-style, after ManualHandoffAimTime [default 0 = immediately]) + anticipatory turn lead — THE death-wobble fix (v0.51: 8 user recordings showed the achieved bank lags the turn-rate bank command by a constant ~0.7s while that command was pure-proportional in the heading error, self-sustaining a 0.3-0.85Hz bank limit cycle at ALL speeds [±88° bank from ±6° aim error, roll railed]; the bank target is now computed from the PREDICTED error azErr - noseHeadingRate*TurnLeadTime [default 0.65s] so it rolls out early instead of after the overshoot; plus AssistOffPitchScale [default 0.5] cuts the instructor's pitch while the game's flight-assist is OFF, where the FBW's stick->rate gain doubles-triples and pitch diverged to AoA ±50°; new CSV columns headingRateFilt/azErrPred) + brake-only lead (v0.52: the v0.51 lead closed its own fast loop — near boresight the prediction was dominated by the heading-rate term, and the speed-scaled bank slope turned ±2°/s of rate ripple into a ±65° bank relay = a NEW 1.1-1.35Hz chatter in HOLD phase [confirmed in 16 v0.51 recordings at 280-510 m/s]; azErrPred is now clamped to [0, azErr] so the lead can roll out early but never command bank past the real error — big turns unchanged, the chatter loop can't self-sustain) + align-hold fine-cone deadzone (v0.53: with the bank pipeline quieted by v0.52, the KR67-class 570+ m/s recordings exposed a SECOND raw-error az→roll path — eAlign=phi/90 is a full-scale directional relay near boresight [phi snaps ±90° with the sign of a sub-degree error] and the align-hold blend weight |azErr|/EvolvedAlignHoldDeg fed it undeadzoned, rocking the wings ±30° at ~1.2Hz while targetBank sat at 0; the weight now subtracts FineBankDeadzone first, same guard the linear bank servo always had, so inside the fine cone roll is purely wings-level + the braked/clamped bank target) + de-rectified lead & slew-limited bank target (v0.54: 19 v0.53 recordings [KR67 450-536 m/s, AB4 Alcyon 226-518 m/s] showed the v0.52 brake-clamp RECTIFYING heading-rate ripple into a 0<->azErr sawtooth on the prediction — azErrPred pinned to exactly 0 while 1.5-5.7° of real error remained, commanding full wings-level mid-correction [the 'self-leveling fights the turn' feel], and the ~44°-bank-per-degree atan slope at 500 m/s turned that sawtooth into a bank target banging 0<->65° at ~1.5Hz that the roll servo faithfully chased [wings rocking ±14-30° from a 1-3° error]; three fixes in the same pipeline: the prediction now floors at 0.30*azErr so level flight is never commanded while error remains [floor self-releases as azErr->0], the heading-rate filter tau rose 0.18->0.35 to cut the ripple feeding the rectifier, and the bank target is slew-limited by new knob BankSlewRate [default 60°/s, 0=off] so it physically can't flap above the airframe's roll response; new CSV column tBankE records the bank target EvolvedLegacy actually flies [the targetBank column is the shared blend it does NOT fly]) + G-LOC fade-to-black warning (v0.55: a gradual full-screen grey-out driven by the same pilotStrength the amber OVER-G text uses, so third-person pilots — who get NONE of the game's cockpit-only black-out — see G-LOC coming instead of an instant control cut at pilotStrength<0.2; all views, late/urgent onset [GLocFadeOnset 0.4] and a heavy-but-not-total 0.7 max grey [GLocFadeMaxAlpha], both live-tunable) + low-speed stall-oscillation fix & stability-assist parity (v0.55: the Draken round-2 report — compounding pitch oscillation below ~450 km/h [AoA swinging -18..+37°, can crash] and assist-OFF turning ~3x slower. Decompiled ControlsFilter.FlyByWire: pitch stick is a g-scaled RATE command [gLimit·9.81/max(V,0.75·Vc)] whose gain collapses below corner speed [×clamp(q_ratio,0.3,1)], while assist OFF at low/mid q swaps in a flat, UNPROTECTED stick·maxPitchAngularVel — identical above ~1.2×Vc q, so v0.51's flat AssistOffPitchScale=0.5 was just halving high-speed assist-off turns and is DELETED. The mod now reads the per-airframe FBW params from the game each airframe [FBW probe: public GetFlyByWireParameters + AccessTools for gLimitPositive/alphaLimiter, fail-soft — helis/disabled FBW keep old behaviour] and: normalizes the pitch command by protected/achievable rate [exactly 1 with assist on or at speed — zero change to the verified high-speed feel; the physically-correct per-airframe cut with assist off at low q]; caps the turn-rate demand omegaDes at the achievable pitch rate in BOTH bank-target sites so low-speed bank targets shrink physically instead of slamming ±72° into a turn the collapsed pitch rate can't fly; freezes the fine integrators while capped [anti-windup — offline fit on the tester CSVs showed corr(command,response) going NEGATIVE below corner speed: the plane had stopped following while the loop kept winding]; and adds a mod-side AoA ceiling at the game's per-airframe alphaLimiter minus 4° [sign-aware so recovery is never blocked, active regardless of assist — assist-OFF gets the protection the game withholds]. New CSV columns assist/fbwTgtPR/fbwPR + a # fbw params header line; analyze-wobble.py gains a per-file stick→rate model fit [high-q/low-q split] and a named low-speed stall-oscillation FAIL verdict) — tune live via F1).
